var tafsirData_72 = {
  "1": "\"Say, ˹O Prophet,˺ “It has been revealed to me that a group of jinn listened ˹to the Quran,˺ and said ˹to their fellow jinn˺, ‘We have indeed heard an amazing recitation—\" opens Surah al-Jinn with a new audience, the jinn, whose listening parallels human listening.\n\n“Say, O Prophet, ‘It has been revealed to me that a group of jinn listened to the Quran, and said to their fellow jinn, We have indeed heard an amazing recitation—’” translates the opening. Revealed to me indicates the Quran, the weighty revelation soon sent, the Reminder that would humble a mountain, the Light that brings from darkness, recited properly in a measured way at night. A group of jinn, or “nafaran mina al-jin,” is a company, as with the helpers and emigrants, but of another creation, created from fire, earlier trying to eavesdrop on heaven with stern guards and shooting stars, now listening to the earthly recitation.\n\nHeard an amazing recitation, or “Qur’anan ‘ajaban,” wondrous, marvelous Quran, like the Gardens’ near fruit and elevated honour, amazing as the seven heavens without flaw and the birds held aloft.\n\nThis follows the spread earth for spacious pathways and walking along them, showing that even jinn walk those pathways and listen.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to treat jinn as folklore. The Quran treats them as accountable, believing or deviant, who will be fuel for Hell or guided to Right Way, similar to humans disbelieving or believing.\n\nFor reflection, be like the group of jinn who listened, were amazed, said it leads to Right Guidance so we believed and will never associate, and recognized the foolish utter falsehoods about Allah. Listen as attentive ears grasp, not as those who pressed fingers and covered clothes, so amazing recitation becomes your right-hand record that says “Read my record,” your life of bliss, and your protection from the Fire that rips scalps and summons hoarders.",
  "2": "\"It leads to Right Guidance so we believed in it, and we will never associate anyone with our Lord ˹in worship˺.\" captures the jinn’s immediate response to hearing the amazing recitation. The amazing Quran was described as leading to “rushd,” sound, right direction.\n\n“It leads to Right Guidance” translates the jinn’s testimony that the recitation guides to uprightness, not to compromise where you soften truth to be yielded to, not to ancient fables dismissal, and not to withholder’s stinginess. Right Guidance is the Straight Path walked upright, the balance so people may administer justice, and the Light that brings from darkness. The jinn recognized it without needing to see the seven heavens flawless or the birds held; they heard and reasoned.\n\n“so we believed in it” shows that guidance was not merely admired, but entered. Believing here is the same belief called after “So believe in Allah and His Messenger and in the Light,” and after “O believers, do not let wealth or children divert.” The jinn believed readily, as with the group that said “We have indeed heard an amazing recitation.”\n\n“and we will never associate anyone with our Lord in worship” is the firm resolve that follows. Association, or “shirk,” includes taking mates and offspring for Allah, seeking refuge with jinn, and invoking others in places of worship that are only for Allah. Never is emphatic, as with the garden owners’ hope “We will never obey anyone against you” was false, but this never is true, spoken by those who submitted and are rightly guided.\n\nThis follows the initial listening to show that listening should lead to joining the party of Allah bound to succeed, not the party of Satan bound to lose.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think jinn belief is different from human belief, requiring different criteria. The Quran presents the same Right Guidance for both, tested by death and life to see best deeds.\n\nFor practice, be like those jinn. When you hear the recitation that the pen writes and the mountain would be humbled by, let it lead you to Right Guidance, believe, and resolve never to associate anyone with your Lord in worship, whether an idol like Wadd or wealth that diverts, so you are among the submitted who have sought the right course and among those given a near fruit that hangs within reach.",
  "3": "\"˹Now, we believe that˺ our Lord—Exalted is His Majesty—has neither taken a mate nor offspring,\" states the jinn’s purified creed after resolving never to associate. The belief corrects falsehoods previously uttered.\n\n“Now, we believe that our Lord—Exalted is His Majesty—has neither taken a mate nor offspring” translates “wa annahu ta‘ala jaddu rabbina ma ittakhadha sahibatan wa la walada.” Exalted is His Majesty, or “ta‘ala jaddu rabbina,” indicates highness of Allah’s grandeur, not a grandfather, but majesty, as with Blessed is the One in Whose Hands rests all authority and Most Capable of everything. Neither mate nor offspring denies the claim that Allah has a partner like the idols’ families, the Christians’ claim about Jesus, or the jinn’s foolish outrageous falsehoods.\n\nThis follows “It leads to Right Guidance so we believed” to show what Right Guidance clarifies, pure monotheism, as with “He is Allah, there is no god except Him, Knower of seen and unseen, Most Compassionate, Most Merciful.”\n\nThe jinn’s correction also mirrors the earlier correction “Your wealth and children are only a test” and “Honour belongs to Allah,” where false attachments are removed.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to read “Exalted is His Majesty” as merely poetic. It is the theological anchor that makes the pen’s oath, the seven heavens without flaw, and the Throne borne by eight coherent.\n\nFor the living, affirming no mate nor offspring shapes practice. Do not seek refuge with jinn, do not invoke anyone besides Allah in places of worship, and do not let wealth or children become partners that divert from remembrance. Affirming this is the Right Guidance that leads to being among those submitted who have sought the right course, whose reward is not fuel for Hell like the deviant, but Gardens where fruit hangs within reach and you are told to eat and drink joyfully.",
  "4": "\"and that the foolish of us used to utter ˹outrageous˺ falsehoods about Allah.\" acknowledges the source of the previous error about mates and offspring. The foolish among jinn and humans had spoken.\n\n“and that the foolish of us used to utter outrageous falsehoods about Allah” translates “wa annahu kana safihuna yaqulu ‘ala Allahi shatatan.” Safih is the foolish, the lightweight, the one who withholds good, transgresses, slanders, as with the despicable oath-taker. Outrageous falsehoods, or “shatat,” are extreme, off-track lies, like saying revelations are ancient fables, pure magic, or poet’s prose, or that oaths bind until the Day whatever you decide, or that associate-gods will intercede.\n\nThe jinn confess that among their own is the foolish who uttered this, just as among humans are the foolish who demanded punishment bound to come and the brute who is despicable and an illegitimate child because blessed with wealth says ancient fables.\n\nThis follows “Exalted is His Majesty has neither mate nor offspring” to show that such claims are foolishness, not knowledge.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think foolishness excuses falsehood. Foolishness explains but does not excuse, as with those who said “if only we had listened and reasoned” after hearing the roar as it boils over. Listening and reasoning are the cure for foolish utterance.\n\nFor practice, do not be among the foolish who utter outrageous falsehoods. Be among the righteous among us and those who are less so but striving, among different factions who have now submitted, who when they heard guidance readily believed and will have no fear of being wronged, so the pen writes your utterance as truth that brings from darkness, not as shatat that summons the raging Flame that rips scalps.\n\nExtra: Outrageous falsehoods also include saying the Quran is ancient fables because blessed with wealth and children, and that oaths bind until the Day whatever you decide. The jinn’s confession that the foolish uttered them shows that even jinn recognize human foolishness can mislead jinn, and jinn foolishness can mislead humans, so seeking Right Guidance must be from the amazing recitation, not from the foolish of either creation, whose party is bound to lose as Satan’s party is bound to lose.",
  "5": "\"We certainly thought that humans and jinn would never speak lies about Allah.\" confesses the jinn’s prior naive trust. The assumption was that neither creation would lie about the Creator.\n\n“We certainly thought that humans and jinn would never speak lies about Allah” translates the jinn’s earlier belief that no one would dare fabricate about Allah. That trust is like the garden owners’ trust that harvest was guaranteed, the hypocrites’ trust that oaths as shields would hold, and the brute’s trust that wealth and children prove ancient fables. The jinn, like humans, assumed that the gravity of speaking about Allah would deter lying, so when the foolish uttered outrageous falsehoods, they were believed.\n\nThis follows the foolish’s utterance to show why it was accepted. The jinn’s thought mirrors human thought that the foolish would not lie about the Most Compassionate who holds birds and smooths earth, so when they did, many were led astray, as with the elite who led many astray and made many think Allah would not resurrect anyone.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think this excuses following lies. The Quran shows that even sincere thought must be tested, as with the test of garden owners and the test where He created death and life to see best deeds.\n\nFor the living, do not assume that no one would lie about Allah. Test speech with Right Guidance, with the pen and what everyone writes, with the flawless heavens, and with the Light. When the foolish says ancient fables or pure magic, recognize it as outrageous, not as truth, and be among those who submitted, whose right course is sought, rather than the deviant who become fuel for Hell, so the terrible thought that no one would lie does not make you fuel.\n\nMore: Never speaking lies about Allah was a naive ideal that revelation corrects, as with the garden owners who thought harvest was guaranteed without “Allah willing” and the hypocrites who thought oaths shield. The jinn’s correction after hearing the amazing recitation shows that naive trust must be replaced by verification through Right Guidance. For the living, do not assume no one would lie about Allah, test every claim that there is no god except Him, that He has no mate nor offspring, and that places of worship are only for Him, so the deviant who becomes fuel for Hell is not followed.",
  "6": "\"And some men used to seek refuge with some jinn—so they increased each other in wickedness.\" describes a mutual corruption between humans and jinn before the Quran’s guidance. The verse explains a pre-Islamic practice.\n\n“And some men used to seek refuge with some jinn—so they increased each other in wickedness” translates a habit where travelers entering a valley would seek protection from the jinn of that place, saying “I seek refuge with the chief of this valley’s jinn.” Some jinn would then increase those men in tyranny, fear, and sin, and the men increased the jinn in arrogance. The increase, or “rahq,” is wrongful exaltation and burden, similar to the despicable withholder who increases delusion and the elite whose wealth increases them in loss.\n\nThis follows the thought that humans and jinn would not lie, to show how seeking refuge with jinn is itself based on lies about Allah, exalting jinn as partners who can protect instead of the Most Compassionate in whom we believe and trust, the Lord of east and west where there is no god except Him so take Him alone as Trustee.\n\nIt also mirrors seeking refuge with strongholds that put them out of reach and honour that expels inferior, all powerless forces that would help instead of the Most Compassionate.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think seeking refuge with jinn is mere superstition without harm. It is shirk that increases wickedness, as with places of worship only for Allah so do not invoke anyone besides Him, and calling only upon my Lord associating none.\n\nFor practice, seek refuge with Allah alone, the King, Holy, Almighty, whose Hands hold authority, who is Most Capable, who smooths earth and holds birds, who is Best Provider of flowing water if yours sinks. That refuge does not increase wickedness but perfects light and admits into Gardens, where the jinn who submitted have sought the right course and the human who submitted will not fear being wronged.",
  "7": "\"And those ˹humans˺ thought, just like you ˹jinn˺, that Allah would not resurrect anyone ˹for judgment˺.\" records another shared misbelief between humans and jinn before guidance.\n\n“And those humans thought, just like you jinn, that Allah would not resurrect anyone for judgment” translates the shared assumption that Allah would not send anyone after death, that no messenger would come, that no gathering like the Day He will gather you all for mutual loss and gain would occur. Humans thought this as with the claim “We will not be resurrected. Yes, by your Lord you will surely be resurrected and that is easy” and the garden owners’ lost way, and jinn thought it as they tried to reach heaven for news and found stern guards.\n\nThis follows seeking refuge with jinn to show that refuge was sought because resurrection was denied, so protection was sought in the present valley rather than in the Lord of pathways where angels ascend on a Day fifty thousand years.\n\nThe shared “just like you” indicates that disbelief in resurrection is not confined to humans, but is a temptation for both creations, as with the despicable who hinders.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to limit resurrection to human bodies. The Quran shows jinn also are accountable, some submitted and some deviant who will be fuel for Hell, so both need warning before painful punishment.\n\nFor reflection, do not think Allah will not resurrect anyone, as that thought makes wealth and children divert, makes wealth merely circulate among rich, and makes you feel secure that earth will not swallow. Instead, firmly believe in the Day of Judgment as the excepted do, who give rightful share, fear punishment knowing none should feel secure, and are properly observant, so resurrection becomes your elevated Garden where you are held in honour, not the raging Flame that rips scalps.",
  "8": "\"˹Earlier˺ we tried to reach heaven ˹for news˺, only to find it filled with stern guards and shooting stars.\" describes the jinn’s experience before the Quran’s arrival, contrasting with earlier seeking refuge.\n\n“Earlier we tried to reach heaven for news, only to find it filled with stern guards and shooting stars” translates the jinn’s attempt to eavesdrop on the unseen, to reach heaven for news of the descent of command between seven heavens. Earlier they used to take positions for eavesdropping, as with devils stoned by lamps as missiles, but now the lowest heaven is filled with stern guards, or “harasan shadidan,” strong, severe guards, and “shuhuban,” flaming shooting stars that lie in wait for any who dares. This is the same guarding that protects the well-preserved Record only purified angels touch and the pen’s truthful writing.\n\nThis follows resurrection denial to show that the unseen is now guarded, so the previous method of seeking news through jinn refuge is closed. The stern guards and shooting stars are the reason “whoever dares eavesdrop now will find a flare lying in wait,” as next verse states.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think guards and stars are mere meteorology. They are created means by the Most Capable who adorns lowest heaven with lamps and makes them missiles for devils.\n\nFor practice, seek news not by eavesdropping with jinn, but by listening to the amazing recitation that leads to Right Guidance, to the weighty revelation soon sent, to the reminder to the whole world. That news is guarded, but offered freely to the mindful, where attentive ears grasp the Ark reminder, not to those who seek refuge with jinn and increase wickedness.\n\nFurther: Stern guards and shooting stars also explain why the well-preserved Record remains well-preserved and why the Pen’s writing remains truthful. Guards are the formidable severe angels who never disobey, like those over the Fire and those bearing the Throne. Their sternness ensures that the Reminder that would humble a mountain remains humble, not tampered. For the listener, stern guards mean the news you need is not stolen via jinn refuge but received via the noble Messenger’s recitation, so take it as weighty revelation soon sent, recite properly in a measured way, and devote yourself wholeheartedly to the Lord of east and west, taking Him alone as Trustee.",
  "9": "\"We used to take up positions there for eavesdropping, but whoever dares eavesdrop now will find a flare lying in wait for them.\" details the former and now blocked access to heavenly news.\n\n“We used to take up positions there for eavesdropping, but whoever dares eavesdrop now will find a flare lying in wait for them” translates the jinn’s confession. Positions, or “maqā‘ida li-s-sama‘,” are seats for hearing, like the worthless planks leaned against a wall that take positions to impress, but here for stealing unseen. Eavesdropping, or “yasmi‘u,” is to hear, as with the amazing recitation heard and the attentive ear that grasps. Now, after the amazing recitation’s arrival, any who dares will find a flare, or “shihab,” a flaming dart lying in wait, as with stern guards and shooting stars.\n\nThis follows stern guards filling heaven to show enforcement. Earlier they tried to reach heaven and found it filled; now they explain the consequence of trying.\n\nThe change, from used to now, marks the Quran’s arrival as turning point, similar to the Ark as reminder and the mountain that would be humbled. Before, jinn could steal fragments; now the well-preserved Record is sealed, and the Reminder is delivered via the noble Messenger whose duty is only to convey, not via stolen whispers.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to romanticize eavesdropping as gaining secret knowledge. The Quran shows it is blocked and now punished, and the true secret, the unseen that none should feel secure from, is disclosed only to chosen messengers with angel-guards before and behind.\n\nFor the living, do not seek eavesdropped news through fortune-tellers whose mumbling the Quran is not, but seek the flare-guarded, angel-delivered recitation that leads to Right Guidance, so you are not like the daring eavesdropper who finds a flare, but like the listening jinn who said “We will never associate” and became among the submitted who sought the right course.",
  "10": "\"Now, we have no clue whether evil is intended for those on earth, or their Lord intends for them what is right.\" voices the jinn’s humility after the heavens were guarded. The admission is honest about limits.\n\n“Now, we have no clue whether evil is intended for those on earth, or their Lord intends for them what is right” translates the jinn’s statement that they do not know if harm is intended for earth’s inhabitants or if their Lord intends right guidance, “rashad,” the same Right Guidance the recitation leads to. Evil here could be swallowing earth as it quakes or stones unleashed if you feel secure, or the severe account for rebellious societies. Right, or “rashad,” is the Straight Path walked upright, the balance so people may administer justice, and the Gardens where the righteous are.\n\nThis follows the flare lying in wait to show that blocked eavesdropping leaves them without stolen news, so they do not claim unseen knowledge, unlike the despicable who claim to have a scripture reading whatever they choose or oaths binding until the Day.\n\nThe statement also mirrors “We used to think humans and jinn would not lie” and “We thought Allah would not resurrect,” now corrected to humble not knowing.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to hear this as doubt in Allah’s mercy. It is the opposite, acknowledging that intention for earth’s people, whether evil as test or right as guidance, belongs to their Lord, the Most Compassionate in whom we believe and trust, whose Hands hold all authority and who is Most Capable.\n\nFor practice, adopt the same humility. Do not claim to know whether the abundant rain after seeking forgiveness is near or the appointed time is delayed, but do know that your Lord intends what is right when you seek His forgiveness, are in awe without seeing, and walk spacious pathways to seek bounty. That humility makes you among those who submit and seek the right course, whose Lord intends for them what is right, not evil.",
  "11": "\"Among us are those who are righteous and those who are less so. We have been of different factions.\" describes the jinn’s internal diversity after admitting limits on earth’s fate.\n\n“Among us are those who are righteous and those who are less so. We have been of different factions” translates “anna minna al-salihuna wa minna duna dhalika, kunna tara’iq qidada,” among us are the righteous and those below that, we have been various paths, splintered. Righteous, or “salihun,” are those who lead to Right Guidance, like the submitted who sought the right course, the mindful who will have Gardens of Bliss, and the excepted who pray consistently. Less so are those less righteous, not yet fully deviant, but not fully submitted, similar to humans divided into believers and disbelievers, submitted and wicked, residents of Fire and Paradise not equal.\n\nDifferent factions, or “tara’iq qidada,” are separate ways, as with hypocrites whose malice for each other is intense though you think they are united, and with the despicable’s many traits. The jinn, like humans, are not monolithic.\n\nThis follows humility about earth’s intention to show that jinn, like humans, are tested, some listening and reasoning, others not, as with “if only we had listened and reasoned.”\n\nA misunderstanding would be to stereotype jinn as only deviant who are fuel for Hell. Some are righteous, some submitted, as next verses say those who submitted have sought the right course.\n\nFor reflection, recognize diversity without stereotyping, whether among jinn or humans. The Garden’s near fruit and elevated honour are for the righteous among us, not for a faction’s name. To be among the righteous, be like the listening group who believed and never associate, who when they heard guidance readily believed and will have no fear of being wronged, so you are not of different factions lost in delusion but of the submitted faction that sought the right course.",
  "12": "\"˹Now,˺ we truly know that we cannot frustrate Allah on earth, nor can we escape from Him ˹into heaven˺.\" states the jinn’s realization of divine inescapability after acknowledging factions.\n\n“Now, we truly know that we cannot frustrate Allah on earth, nor can we escape from Him into heaven” translates the jinn’s certainty that they cannot impossibly hinder Allah on earth nor flee to heaven to escape, as with “No calamity befalls except by Allah’s Will” and “He knows whatever you conceal and reveal.” Cannot frustrate, or “lan nu‘jiza,” is to be unable to make helpless, as with the Inevitable Hour seen as far but near with Allah, and as with the challenger demanding punishment bound to come averted by none. Nor can we escape into heaven, or “haraban,” fleeing, as with the flare lying in wait for eavesdroppers and stern guards filling heaven.\n\nNow, or emphasis, indicates this knowledge came after hearing the amazing recitation that leads to Right Guidance, not before, when they tried to reach heaven and found guards.\n\nThis follows among us are righteous and less so to show that knowledge of inescapability should lead to choosing righteousness, as with the submitted who sought right course.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to hear this as fatalism. Inescapability is about accountability, not about losing the ability to seek forgiveness and Gardens, which remain.\n\nFor practice, know you cannot frustrate Allah on earth by withholding good, by saying ancient fables, or by feeling secure that earth will not swallow, nor escape into heaven by eavesdropping. Instead, frustrate not, but submit, believe when you hear guidance, have no fear of being wronged, and be among those who pray consistently, give rightful share, and walk upright, so inescapability becomes nearness to the Most Compassionate who holds birds and smooths earth for you, whose Hands hold all authority and whose punishment none should feel secure from is averted for you.",
  "13": "\"When we heard the guidance ˹of the Quran˺, we ˹readily˺ believed in it. For whoever believes in their Lord will have no fear of being wronged ˹in reward˺ or denied ˹it˺.\" describes the jinn’s faith after realizing inescapability. The response is immediate belief.\n\n“When we heard the guidance of the Quran, we readily believed in it. For whoever believes in their Lord will have no fear of being wronged or denied it” translates the jinn’s testimony. Guidance, or “huda,” is the amazing recitation that leads to Right Guidance, the Light that brings from darkness, the Reminder that would humble a mountain, recited by the noble Messenger. Readily believed indicates no delay like pressing fingers and covering clothes, but like attentive ears that grasp the Ark reminder.\n\n“Whoever believes in their Lord will have no fear of being wronged or denied it” translates “fa-man yu’min bi-rabbihi fa-la yakhafu bakhsan wa la rahqan,” no fear of diminishment of reward or of burden beyond what is due. No fear of being wronged or denied is the counterpart to “No calamity befalls except by Allah’s Will and whoever has faith, He will guide their hearts,” and to the Pen’s accurate writing. It assures that faith is not lost, as with the good loan multiplied and forgiven by the Most Appreciative, Most Forbearing.\n\nThis follows inescapability to show that the only escape from inescapability is belief, not flight.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think belief guarantees no test. Belief guarantees no wrong in reward, not no test, as with wealth and children are only a test but Allah has great reward.\n\nFor the living, hear guidance as the jinn did, believe readily, and trust that the Knower of seen and unseen, Most Subtle, All-Aware, who knows whether you speak secretly or openly, will not wrong your reward, so the garden owners’ hope for a better garden after turning becomes your certainty of an elevated Garden where fruit hangs within reach and you are told to eat and drink joyfully.",
  "14": "\"And among us are those who have submitted ˹to Allah˺ and those who are deviant. So ˹as for˺ those who submitted, it is they who have sought the right course.\" classifies the jinn after believing, sorting submitted and deviant, and defining the submitted’s achievement.\n\n“And among us are those who have submitted to Allah and those who are deviant. So as for those who submitted, it is they who have sought the right course” translates “wa anna minna al-muslimuna wa minna al-qasitun, fa-man aslama fa-ula’ika taharraw rashada,” among us are the muslims and the deviants, and whoever has submitted has sought Right Guidance. Muslim here is one who submits, as with those who submitted not treated like wicked, and as with the exception of the deviant who will be fuel for Hell.\n\nDeviant, or “qasitun,” is one who deviates, unjust, as with the despicable, the hypocrites, and those who turned backs and hoarded. Submitted sought the right course, or “taharraw rashada,” actively pursued the Right Guidance, as with the helpers who loved emigrants and the disciples who stood with Jesus.\n\nThis follows readily believing and having no fear of being wronged, to show that submitting is the purposeful pursuit after belief.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think submitted is a label without pursuit. Taharraw indicates seeking, striving, as with striving with wealth and lives as best for you.\n\nFor practice, be among those who have submitted and have sought the right course. Seek it by listening to the amazing recitation, by being in awe without seeing, by protecting families, and by being true to trusts, so the deviant’s fuel for Hell is avoided and the submitted’s right course leads to Gardens held in honour where no close friend fails and the raging Flame does not summon.\n\nAdditional: Submitted, or “muslimun,” among jinn parallels among humans those who have submitted not treated like the wicked, whose Gardens of Bliss are distinguished, whose reward is not fuel. Submitted among jinn sought the right course, or “taharraw rashada,” actively pursued, as with the helpers who loved emigrants and preferred them despite need, and the disciples who stood with Jesus. Seeking indicates that submission is not passive label but pursuit, as with striving with wealth and lives as best for you, and competing for forgiveness and Paradise as vast as heavens and earth. Pursue it, so you are among the submitted, not the deviant.",
  "15": "\"And as for the deviant, they will be fuel for Hell.”\" states the counterpart for the deviant among jinn. The verse is stark and matches human deviant.\n\n“And as for the deviant, they will be fuel for Hell” translates “wa amma al-qasituna fa-kanu li-jahannama hataba,” the deviant will be firewood for Hell. Fuel, or “hatab,” is what feeds the Flame that rips scalps, the raging Flame, the Blaze that almost bursts, the choking food, and the painful punishment in store. Fuel is the opposite of the right course sought by the submitted. It mirrors “they will be fuel for Hell” for humans who hinder, withhold, and deny, and “they will be residents of the Fire, staying there forever, what an evil destination,” and “no food except oozing pus which none eat except evildoers.”\n\nThis follows submitted have sought the right course to show the divergent paths, submitted to Gardens, deviant to fuel.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think this is ethnic fate for jinn. It is the choice of deviating after hearing guidance, as with the jinn who thought humans and jinn would not lie and who sought refuge with jinn, now corrected.\n\nFor reflection, avoid being deviant by not being among those who speak outrageous falsehoods, who think Allah will not resurrect, who seek refuge with jinn, and who eavesdrop. Instead, when you hear guidance of the Quran, readily believe, have no fear of being wronged, submit and seek right course, so you are not fuel for Hell but among those in whose wealth is a known right for asker and deprived, whose light shines ahead, and whose Gardens are held in honour.\n\nMore: Fuel for Hell as “hatab” also recalls the Fire’s fuel being people and stones, the shackles, raging Fire, choking food, and painful punishment in store, and the dunes of shifting sand on the Day earth and mountains shake. Fuel is what sustains the Fire, showing that the deviant not only suffers but feeds the suffering of others, as with the withholder who increases delusion and the elite whose wealth increases only in loss. To avoid being fuel, be among the submitted who sought the right course, whose wealth is a known right for the asker and deprived, whose Gardens are held in honour and whose fruit hangs within reach.",
  "16": "\"Had the deniers followed the Right Way, We would have certainly granted them abundant rain to drink—\" offers hypothetical mercy after sorting submitted and deviant, deviant as fuel for Hell. The verse shows what would have been.\n\n“Had the deniers followed the Right Way, We would have certainly granted them abundant rain to drink—” translates “wa an law istaqamu ‘ala al-tariqati la-asqaynahum ma’an ghadaqa,” had they remained straight on the way, We would have given them water abundant to drink. Right Way, or “tariqah,” is the Straight Path walked upright, the Balance so people may administer justice, the Light, the Pen’s writing, the Friday call. Abundant rain to drink echoes “He will shower you with abundant rain” promised to Noah’s people if they seek forgiveness, and “if your water were to sink, who else could bring you flowing water?” and the Gardens and rivers supplied with wealth and children.\n\nThis follows deviant as fuel to show that the same deniers could have had rain.\n\nA test follows, as next verse says “as a test for them. And whoever turns away from remembrance will be admitted into overwhelming punishment.” Rain is test, as wealth and children are test.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to see rain as guarantee of piety’s ease. Rain is also test of best deeds, as with the garden test as We tested Meccans and owners who swore to harvest without “Allah willing” and found ashes.\n\nFor practice, follow the Right Way, seek forgiveness, be mindful to best ability, hear and obey, spend, so abundant rain to drink becomes Gardens and rivers not only in this world but in the Hereafter where fruit hangs within reach, and you are not fuel for Hell but submitted who sought right course and whose reward is not withheld.\n\nFurther: Abundant rain to drink as “ma’an ghadaqa,” copious water to drink, also connects to the flowing water that will be brought if yours sinks, the rain He will shower with abundant rain after seeking forgiveness, and the rivers given with gardens. Drinking indicates satisfaction, as with the choking food and painful punishment in store, abundant rain’s opposite is the garden reduced to ashes while they slept. Had they followed the Right Way, rain would be mercy, not flood, test, not tyranny. To receive it, follow Right Way, be mindful to best ability, hear and obey, spend, and protect families, so rain becomes Gardens and rivers in this world and flowing rivers under Gardens for ever and ever in the next.",
  "17": "\"as a test for them. And whoever turns away from the remembrance of their Lord will be admitted by Him into an overwhelming punishment\" explains the purpose of abundant rain and the consequence of turning from remembrance.\n\n“as a test for them. And whoever turns away from the remembrance of their Lord will be admitted by Him into an overwhelming punishment” translates “li-naftinahum fihi, wa man yu‘rid ‘an dhikri rabbihi yaslukhu ‘adhaban sa‘ada,” to test them therein, and whoever turns from his Lord’s remembrance, He will drive him into a punishment ascending, overwhelming. Test, or “naftinahum,” is as with “We have tested as We tested the garden owners” and “He created death and life to test which is best in deeds.” Rain, wealth, children, gardens, rivers are tests, not entitlements, similar to the challenger demanding punishment.\n\nTurning away from remembrance, or “dhikr,” is the opposite of being humbled when Allah is remembered, of remembering the Name wholeheartedly, and of attentive ears grasping the Ark reminder. Remembrance here is the Quran, the Light, the weighty revelation soon sent, the pen’s writing.\n\nOverwhelming punishment, or “‘adhaban sa‘ada,” is ascending, mounting torment, as with the raging Flame that rips scalps, the Fire nearly bursting, and the severe punishment prepared. Ascending indicates it grows, like mountains crushed then dunes, like sky torn.\n\nThis follows abundant rain to show that rain’s abundance does not guarantee safety; response does.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think turning away is minor neglect. It is the root of hoarding and turning backs that the Flame summons.\n\nFor the living, be tested with rain and turn not away, but remember often after dispersing to seek bounty after Friday, be among those in awe without seeing whose mighty reward is forgiveness, so the test becomes elevation to Gardens held in honour, not an overwhelming punishment that ascends.",
  "18": "\"The places of worship are ˹only˺ for Allah, so do not invoke anyone besides Him.\" states the principle after warning of overwhelming punishment for turning from remembrance. The verse defines the purpose of mosques.\n\n“The places of worship are only for Allah, so do not invoke anyone besides Him” translates “wa anna al-masajida lillahi fa-la tad‘u ma‘a Allahi ahadan,” the mosques belong to Allah, so call not with Allah anyone. Masajid are places of prostration, as with being called to prostrate when fully capable but choosing not to, and the Day the Shin is bared and they are asked to prostrate but cannot. Only for Allah indicates that invocation, or “du‘a,” worship, is exclusive, as with “I call only upon my Lord, associating none with Him” next, and “Say, it is not in my power to harm or benefit you; no one can protect me from Allah nor can I find refuge other than Him.”\n\nThis follows the test of rain and overwhelming punishment to show that remembrance’s proper place is worship for Allah, not seeking refuge with jinn, not urging idols Wadd and Nasr, not believing Allah has mate or offspring.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to limit places of worship to buildings. Masajid includes every place of prostration, as the Pen writes, as the smoothed earth you move about is also for remembrance often.\n\nFor practice, make your places of worship only for Allah, whether the mosque on Friday where you proceed diligently and leave business, or the night prayer where you stand for two-thirds and recite properly. Do not invoke jinn, idols, or powerless forces that would help instead of the Most Compassionate, so your invocation is heard by the All-Aware who knows whether you speak secretly or openly, and your Gardens remain held in honour, not fuel for Hell.",
  "19": "\"Yet when the servant of Allah stood up calling upon Him ˹alone˺, the pagans almost swarmed over him.\" describes the reaction to exclusive worship just commanded. The servant is Muhammad.\n\n“Yet when the servant of Allah stood up calling upon Him alone, the pagans almost swarmed over him” translates the scene when the Prophet stood to call upon his Lord alone, associating none, the pagans gathered around him in crowds to overwhelm, as with rushing headlong from right and left in groups to mock and eyes that would almost cut you down when they hear the Reminder. Stood up calling indicates the Prophet’s night worship standing and his public calling, as with the servant of Allah stood up calling, the weighty revelation soon sent.\n\nAlmost swarmed, or “kadu yakununa ‘alayhi libada,” they were near to be upon him like a compacted mass, similar to the despicable’s slander and gossip that swarms.\n\nThis follows places of worship only for Allah to show that calling upon Him alone provokes the devotees of idols and merchandise fanfare, as with the garden owners’ fixation and the challenger demanding punishment.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to see swarming as success for pagans. The Quran says almost, but the Lord of pathways protects, the pen writes, and the Reminder is for the whole world, so swarming fails.\n\nFor the Prophet and believers, this verse encourages beautiful patience, not like Jonah, continuing to call only upon my Lord, so the swarming becomes the Day they will know who is weaker in helpers and inferior in manpower, while the servant’s Gardens remain held in honour and his never-ending reward remains.\n\nExtra: Swarmed over him also recalls rushing headlong from right and left in groups to mock and eyes that would almost cut you down when they hear the Reminder. Swarming is the powerless force’s attempt to overwhelm the servant who calls upon Him alone, similar to the despicable oath-taker, slanderer, gossip-monger, withholder, transgressor, brute who try to overwhelm. Almost indicates they did not succeed, as with the Inevitable’s one blast that they see as far but We see as near, and the Lord of pathways’ protection. Endurance with beautiful patience, not like Jonah in distress, keeps the servant standing, so swarming becomes the Day they will know who is weaker in helpers and inferior in manpower, while the servant’s Gardens remain held in honour.",
  "20": "\"Say, ˹O Prophet,˺ “I call only upon my Lord, associating none with Him ˹in worship˺.”\" gives the response to swarming. The Prophet is told to declare exclusive calling.\n\n“Say, O Prophet, ‘I call only upon my Lord, associating none with Him in worship’” translates the declaration of pure monotheism after swarming. I call only upon my Lord, or “ad‘u rabbī,” is the same call as places of worship only for Allah, so do not invoke anyone besides Him, and as the jinn’s “we will never associate anyone with our Lord.” Associating none, or “la ushriku bihi ahadan,” denies mate, offspring, idols, jinn refuge, and wealth as partner that diverts.\n\nThis follows swarming to show that swarming does not change calling. The Prophet, of outstanding character, not insane, with never-ending reward, stands calling upon his Lord alone, as the disciples stood with Jesus, as the helpers stood with the emigrants.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to hear this as isolation. Calling only upon my Lord is the most connected act, to the One who holds birds, smooths earth, and descends command between seven heavens.\n\nFor believers, say the same. When you pray consistently and properly observant, when you give rightful share to the asker and deprived, say “I call only upon my Lord, associating none,” so the swarming that almost covered him does not cover you, and the Day the sky is molten brass finds you with light ahead, not with eyes downcast covered with disgrace.\n\nMore: Calling only upon my Lord also echoes the earlier places of worship only for Allah, so do not invoke anyone besides Him, and the King, Holy, source of Serenity who is to be invoked. Only upon my Lord is the opposite of seeking refuge with jinn, urging idols Wadd and Nasr, and believing Allah has mate or offspring. It is the pure monotheism that the jinn confessed as “Exalted is His Majesty” and will never associate. For practice, call only upon Him when you fear punishment knowing none should feel secure, when you guard chastity, keep trusts, and are properly observant, so calling becomes your light ahead and your Garden’s near fruit.",
  "21": "\"Say, “It is not in my power to harm or benefit you.”\" continues the declarations after “I call only upon my Lord.” The verse defines the Messenger’s limits.\n\n“Say, ‘It is not in my power to harm or benefit you’” translates the Prophet’s statement that harm and benefit, or “darr and rashad,” guidance vs harm, are not in his hand, but in Allah’s, the Lord of pathways, the Most Capable, the King, Holy who knows whatever you conceal and reveal. This mirrors “It is not in my power to harm or benefit you” as with “No one can protect me from Allah nor can I find refuge other than Him” and “My duty is only to convey from Allah.”\n\nThis follows calling only upon my Lord to show that the caller is not a deity who controls, but a servant who delivers the weighty revelation, recites properly, and is patient with what they say.\n\nThe statement counters both the expectation that the Prophet could avert the punishment demanded by the challenger averted by none, and the fear that his calling brings harm via swarming.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think this diminishes the Prophet. It elevates him as trustworthy, not claiming what is Allah’s, as with the pen’s truthful writing and the well-preserved Record only purified touch.\n\nFor the community, this teaches proper reliance. Do not seek harm or benefit from the Messenger as if he were associate-god to bring forth; seek from the Lord of all worlds whose Treasuries belong to Him yet hypocrites do not comprehend, whose Hands hold all authority. That reliance makes you among the submitted who sought the right course, not the deviant fuel for Hell who sought refuge with jinn.\n\nFurther: Not in my power to harm or benefit also explains why the Messenger does not ask for a reward so they would be overburdened by debt, and why he does not have unseen Record to copy. Harm and benefit, or “darr and rashad,” are with Allah, the Knower of unseen who discloses none except to chosen messengers with angel-guards before and behind. The Messenger’s not having power is not weakness, but trustworthiness, as with the pen that writes truthfully and the well-preserved Record only purified touch. To seek harm or benefit, turn to the Lord of all worlds whose Hands hold all authority and who is Most Capable of everything, who created death and life to test, and who will admit the righteous into Gardens of Bliss.",
  "22": "\"Say, “No one can protect me from Allah ˹if I were to disobey Him˺, nor can I find any refuge other than Him.\" continues the Prophet’s declarations of limits. After saying it is not in his power to harm or benefit, he states that no protector exists against Allah.\n\n“No one can protect me from Allah if I were to disobey Him, nor can I find any refuge other than Him” translates the Prophet’s acknowledgment that even he, the noble Messenger not insane, of outstanding character, with never-ending reward, is accountable. Protection, or “yujir,” is to grant refuge, as with seeking refuge with jinn which increased wickedness, and seeking refuge with strongholds that put them out of reach, and honour that expels inferior. None can protect the disobedient, as with none can shield him from Us in the hypothetical severing of the aorta, and none can avert punishment for disbelievers from the Lord of pathways.\n\nThis follows harm or benefit to show that the Messenger’s lack of power includes lack of self-protection, so his trust is in Allah, the Most Compassionate in whom we believe and trust, the Lord of east and west whose Trustee he takes.\n\nThe phrase “if I were to disobey Him” is hypothetical for the protected Prophet, but real for others who disobey and are deviant, fuel for Hell, and who turn away from remembrance into overwhelming punishment.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think this diminishes the Prophet’s intercession. Intercession is by Allah’s permission for the mindful, not protection against Allah.\n\nFor believers, this teaches that no close friend will ask on the Day, no clan that sheltered will help, and everyone on earth cannot ransom, so refuge must be sought now with Allah alone, before the Day the sky is molten brass and mountains are wool, by being among those who pray consistently, give rightful share, and are properly observant, whose Gardens are held in honour.",
  "23": "\"˹My duty is˺ only to convey ˹the truth˺ from Allah and ˹deliver˺ His messages.” And whoever disobeys Allah and His Messenger will certainly be in the Fire of Hell, to stay there forever.”\" defines the Messenger’s role and the consequence of disobeying.\n\n“My duty is only to convey the truth from Allah and deliver His messages” translates “illa balaghan min Allahi wa risalatihi,” except a conveyance from Allah and His messages. Duty is only to convey, as with “Our Messenger’s duty is only to deliver clearly,” with the pen and what everyone writes, with the Reminder for the whole world, and with the weighty revelation soon sent. Conveyance includes reciting properly in a measured way, purifying, teaching Book and wisdom, as with the illiterate messenger. Only to convey indicates he is not a protector, not a provider of harm or benefit, but a deliverer, as with “Say, I do not know if what you are promised is near or distant.”\n\n“And whoever disobeys Allah and His Messenger will certainly be in the Fire of Hell, to stay there forever” states the outcome for rejecting the conveyance, paralleling the deviant fuel for Hell and the overwhelming punishment for turning from remembrance. Fire of Hell, or “nar Jahannam,” is the raging Flame that rips scalps, the Blaze that almost bursts, the choking food and painful punishment in store, now named as eternal for the disobedient who persist, not for the mindful who are taught.\n\nThis follows no protector nor refuge to show that disobedience has no alternate shelter.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think conveying is passive. Conveying includes warning before painful punishment as Noah did day and night, openly, publicly, privately, and calling to seek forgiveness.\n\nFor practice, receive the conveyance, believe in the Messenger and in the Light, and do not disobey by hindering with false shields, withholding good, or calling ancient fables. Instead, obey, be true to trusts, honest in testimony, and properly observant, so conveyance becomes your Gardens held in honour, not the Fire where the disobedient will stay forever, and where no close friend helps.",
  "24": "\"Only when they see what they have been threatened with will they know who is weaker in helpers and inferior in manpower.\" describes when the mockers’ swarming will be exposed. The “only when they see” indicates delayed realization.\n\n“Only when they see what they have been threatened with will they know who is weaker in helpers and inferior in manpower” translates the time when the promised threat, the Inevitable Hour, the Striking Disaster, the Day they come forth racing to an idol with eyes downcast covered with disgrace, the Fire that summons, becomes visible. Weaker in helpers, or “ad‘afu nasiran,” fewer supporters, and inferior in manpower, or “aqallu ‘adada,” fewer numbers, contrasts with their swarming over the servant, their rushing headlong in groups to mock, their boasting honour will expel inferior, and their challenge demanding punishment bound to come.\n\nThis follows “My duty is only to convey” and “whoever disobeys will be in Fire forever” to show that conveyance warns of a Day when helper counts are reversed, similar to soon you and the pagans will see which is mad, and they see it as far but We see it as near.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think helpers and numbers decide truth. Helpers here are not tribal numbers, but the党 of Allah bound to succeed, whose helpers are the submitted who sought right course, whose rightful share was given, and whose light shines ahead.\n\nFor reflection, choose helpers now that will not be weaker then. Help instead of the Most Compassionate is delusion; help of the Most Compassionate is the Lord of pathways, the Knower of unseen who discloses to chosen messengers with angel-guards. Be among the helpers of Allah as disciples stood with Jesus, as helpers loved emigrants, so when you see what you were threatened with, you know you are not weaker but held in honour in Gardens where fruit hangs within reach.",
  "25": "\"Say, “I do not know if what you are promised is near or my Lord has set a distant time for it.\" acknowledges limits on knowledge of timing after stating that only when they see the threat will they know who is weaker.\n\n“Say, I do not know if what you are promised is near or my Lord has set a distant time for it” translates the Prophet’s statement about the promised punishment and gathering. Near, or “qarib,” and distant, or “amadan ba‘ida,” are relative, as with the Day fifty thousand years, the challenger’s demand for near punishment, and they see it as far but We see it as near. The Prophet, though a noble Messenger of outstanding character, does not claim to know if the Inevitable’s one blast, the Trumpet, the crushing, or the swallowing and stones are near in worldly terms or distant by Allah’s Will, where every calamity or blessing is written before creation and the appointed time never delays.\n\nThis follows weaker in helpers to show that timing does not affect truth, and precedes the Knower of the unseen who discloses none except to chosen messengers with guards.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to treat not knowing as lack of prophethood, as with how can humans be guides? Not knowing the unseen’s timing is part of being a warner, not a fortune-teller whose mumbling the Quran is not.\n\nFor believers, “I do not know if near or distant” teaches beautiful patience with the Lord’s decree, not like Jonah in distress, and not to demand dates as the deniers did with “When will this threat come?” Instead, be patient, be among those who pray consistently, give rightful share, and walk upright, so whether near or distant, you are ready, and the Day fifty thousand years is for you like light ahead, not like the raging Flame that rips scalps.",
  "26": "\"˹He is the˺ Knower of the unseen, disclosing none of it to anyone,\" defines the source of timing knowledge. The verse follows “I do not know if near or distant” to explain why.\n\n“He is the Knower of the unseen, disclosing none of it to anyone” translates “‘alimu al-ghayb fa-la yuzhiru ‘ala ghaybihi ahadan,” Knower of the unseen, the well-preserved Record only purified touch, the appointed time that never delays, the Day the Shin is bared, the Throne borne by eight, the Flames’s ripping and summoning. Unseen, or “ghayb,” is what is hidden, like whether you speak secretly or openly He knows best what is hidden in the heart, and the seen and unseen He knows. Disclosing none to anyone indicates that the unseen is not accessible via eavesdropping jinn who now find a flare lying in wait, nor via seeking refuge with jinn, nor via poet or fortune-teller.\n\nThis follows the Prophet’s not knowing to show that even he does not disclose unseen except as permitted next.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think this denies revelation altogether. Revelation is disclosed to chosen messengers, as next verse states.\n\nFor practice, do not seek the unseen via despicable oath-taker, slanderer, or ancient fables dismissal. Seek it via the Knower who discloses to His chosen, whose weighty revelation soon sent is recited properly, whose Reminder is for the whole world, and whose pen writes truth. That seeking makes you among the submitted who sought right course, not the deviant fuel for Hell who sought refuge with jinn and increased wickedness.\n\nExtra: Knower of the unseen also explains why the well-preserved Record remains well-preserved and why the pen writes truthfully. The unseen includes the appointed time that never delays, the Day fifty thousand years, and the provision from sources never imagined. Disclosing none to anyone except chosen messengers means the unseen is not for fortune-tellers whose mumbling the Quran is not, nor for those who claim to copy the Record. To access it, follow the chosen messenger who recites the weighty revelation, stands at night properly, and is guarded before and behind, so your guidance is not stolen like eavesdropping jinn’s flare, but delivered as light that perfects and Gardens that remain.",
  "27": "\"except messengers of His choice. Then He appoints angel-guards before and behind them\" gives the exception to unseen disclosure. The verse shows how revelation reaches safely.\n\n“except messengers of His choice. Then He appoints angel-guards before and behind them” translates that the Knower discloses unseen only to messengers He chooses, then sets guards front and back. Messengers of His choice include Noah sent to warn, the illiterate messenger reciting, purifying, teaching, and the noble Messenger whose recitation is not poet or fortune-teller, whose outstanding character and never-ending reward prove sincerity. Angel-guards, or “rasada,” are stern guards like those filling heaven with shooting stars, formidable severe angels who never disobey, who guard the lowest heaven with lamps as missiles, and who will bear the Throne.\n\nThis follows Knower disclosing none to show that disclosure is not open, but guarded, ensuring that what the Pen writes and the well-preserved Record holds remains uncorrupted, and that had the Messenger made up something, he would have been seized by the right hand and aorta and none could shield.\n\nGuards before and behind indicate complete protection, as with the Lord of east and west taken as Trustee and the weighty revelation’s proper recitation at night.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think guards imply messengers are distrusted. Guards protect the message from being stolen by eavesdropping jinn or altered by hoarders.\n\nFor believers, this guarding assures that the amazing recitation heard by the jinn and that leads to Right Guidance is authentic, so believing in it and never associating is sound, and whoever believes will have no fear of being wronged. Trust the guarded conveyance, follow the Right Way to be granted abundant rain to drink as a test you will pass, and keep places of worship only for Allah, so your guidance is not from deviant fuel but from the submitted right course.",
  "28": "\"to ensure that the messengers fully deliver the messages of their Lord—though He ˹already˺ knows all about them, and keeps account of everything.\" states the purpose of angel-guards before and behind messengers.\n\n“to ensure that the messengers fully deliver the messages of their Lord—though He already knows all about them, and keeps account of everything” translates “li-ya‘lama an qad ablaghu risalati rabbihim wa ahata bi-ma ladayhim wa ahsa kulla shay’in ‘adada,” that it may be known they have delivered their Lord’s messages, while He encompasses what is with them and has enumerated everything in number. Ensure delivery is the guards’ role, as with the pen that writes what everyone writes and the well-preserved Record. Though He already knows about them, or “ahata bi-ma ladayhim,” He encompasses what is with them, as with the Most Subtle, All-Aware, the Knower of seen and unseen who knows whether you speak secretly or openly, and as with the Lord who descends command between seven heavens so you may know He is Most Capable and encompasses all knowledge.\n\nKeeps account of everything, or “ahsa kulla shay’in ‘adada,” He has counted everything in number, as with every calamity or blessing written before creation where that is easy, and He will inform you of what you have done and that is easy.\n\nThis follows guards to show that guarding is not for Allah’s knowledge, which already encompasses, but for clear delivery and witnessing, like the two witnesses bearing true testimony for Allah in divorce.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think “to ensure that the messengers deliver” implies doubt about the messengers. It is to make evident to all, including the jinn who listened and the humans who rushed to mock, that delivery was complete, removing excuse “Did a warner not come?” on the Day.\n\nFor practice, trust that delivery is ensured, so receive it. Believe in the Light, be among those who give rightful share, are true to trusts, and are properly observant, so the account kept of everything counts you among those held in honour in Gardens, where you are told to eat and drink joyfully, not among the deviant counted as fuel for Hell."
};